From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:37:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 25/28] fix(mcp): name the configured origin on the public
 host, not the proxy's scheme
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The OAuth protected-resource metadata, the authorization-server bridge and
the MCP 401 challenge built their origin from req.protocol. Behind a proxy
that speaks plain http to doop and sets (or overwrites) X-Forwarded-Proto to
http while clients use https, every one of them said http://<host>/mcp, and
strict MCP clients refuse a resource that differs from the https URL they
called (RFC 9728 §3.3), so connecting an agent failed.

server/requestOrigin.ts: a request for BETTER_AUTH_URL's host gets
BETTER_AUTH_URL's own origin; any other host (dev on :4300/:4301/:4400, an
alias) is echoed from the request exactly as before, so those still validate.

Test (tests/access.test.ts): with X-Forwarded-Proto: https on the configured
http://localhost:<port>, the metadata and the challenge name the configured
origin (before: https://localhost:<port>/mcp), and a request on 127.0.0.1 is
still echoed as 127.0.0.1.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
